WEBVTT

00:00:00.485 --> 00:00:03.972
PostgreSQL supports a security invoker option for views.

00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:09.137
With security invoker, permissions on underlying relations are checked using the invoking user's rights.

00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:13.102
This can matter in a real multi-role security design.

00:00:13.102 --> 00:00:19.337
Our browser lab is useful for syntax and object behavior, but it does not reproduce a full production

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:23.982
authorization environment. Views can reduce exposure by presenting only approved columns or rows,

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:29.372
but they are not a complete security strategy by themselves.

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:34.567
Understand ownership, privileges, and whether the view executes with invoker or definer-like behavior.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.393
Sensitive data controls should be explicit and tested.
